Package: mlesky
Type: Package
Title: Maximum Likelihood Phylodynamic Inference of Population Size
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
	person("Erik", "Volz", email = "erik.volz@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
	, person("Xavier", "Didelot", role = "aut")
	, person("Vinicius", "Franceschi", role = "ctb")
	)
Description: Maximum likelihood estimation of effective population size
    through time, growth rates, and phylodynamic regressions with
    non-genetic covariate time series, from one or more dated phylogenies.
    Skygrid, skygrowth and skykappa models are implemented, a
    likelihood-based cross-validation technique is used to choose the
    smoothing parameter, and the resolution of the time grid can be chosen
    by AIC or BIC. Coalescent simulators with time-varying population size
    are included for parametric bootstrapping. The methods are described in
    Didelot et al. (2023) <doi:10.1093/ve/vead028>.
